menu "CYB3RGUN pistol stub"

config CGPISTOL_CHANNEL
    int "Fixed 2.4 GHz channel"
    range 1 13
    default 1
    help
        Must match the module's channel. The module keeps its channel in
        NVS and takes it from the core; the stub has no core, so it is set
        here.

config CGPISTOL_SLOT
    int "Slot this stub aims at"
    range 0 32
    default 1
    help
        The multiplex slot the pistol believes it identified. 0 means no
        beacons were identified, which every module acknowledges and
        forwards as unaimed.

config CGPISTOL_AUTOFIRE
    bool "Fire on a timer as well as on the button"
    default y
    help
        A bench run needs a steady stream of shots. Turn this off to fire
        only with the PRG button.

config CGPISTOL_RATE_MS
    int "Milliseconds between shots when firing on the timer"
    range 10 60000
    default 200
    help
        200 ms is five shots a second, so a run of 100 shots takes about
        twenty seconds.

config CGPISTOL_ACK_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "Milliseconds to wait for the module's acknowledgement"
    range 2 1000
    default 20
    help
        concept.md principle 1 puts the radio round trip in single digit
        milliseconds, so 20 ms is generous and still lets all four
        transmissions of one shot finish inside 80 ms.

config CGPISTOL_RUN_SHOTS
    int "Shots per run, 0 to never summarise"
    range 0 100000
    default 100
    help
        The summary is printed when the run completes. S01-B01 asks for
        100 shots per distance.

config CGPISTOL_TRACE
    bool "Print one line per shot"
    default n
    help
        Useful when a single exchange misbehaves, too noisy for a run.

endmenu
